Evidence C - release 2026.10.26-2:
// lib/dashboard.ts (PR #611)
export async function getDashboard() {
  const session = await getSession();             // reads the session cookie
  return cached("dashboard", 60, () => db.dashboardFor(session.userId));
}

// app/api/dashboard/route.ts (PR #612)
export async function GET() {
  const session = await getSession();
  if (!session) return Response.json({ error: "sign in" }, { status: 401, headers: { "Cache-Control": "private, no-store" } });
  return Response.json(await getDashboard(), { headers: { "Cache-Control": "public, s-maxage=60" } });
}

Evidence D - timeline:
Mon 17:40  deploy 2026.10.26-2 (PR #611, PR #612)
Mon 17:41  origin requests to /api/dashboard drop from ~1,900/min to ~30/min
Tue 08:55  instructor publishes an edit to "SQL Basics" (typo in a lesson title)
Tue 09:12  ticket #5120
Tue 09:20  ticket #5124
Tue 09:34  on-call purges /api/dashboard at the CDN and adds a CDN rule: BYPASS /api/dashboard
Tue 09:36  ticket #5131
Tue 09:40  auth log, 09:30-09:40: every /api/dashboard request authenticated as the user of its own session cookie; 0 session errors

Statement: "Both layers can serve one learner's dashboard to another on their own: the data cache keys the result as \"dashboard\" without the user id, and public, s-maxage=60 lets the CDN share it by URL; ticket #5131, after the CDN bypass at 09:34, is the leak of the data cache alone."

Evidence C - release 2026.10.26-2:
// lib/dashboard.ts (PR #611)
export async function getDashboard() {
  const session = await getSession();             // reads the session cookie
  return cached("dashboard", 60, () => db.dashboardFor(session.userId));
}

// app/api/dashboard/route.ts (PR #612)
export async function GET() {
  const session = await getSession();
  if (!session) return Response.json({ error: "sign in" }, { status: 401, headers: { "Cache-Control": "private, no-store" } });
  return Response.json(await getDashboard(), { headers: { "Cache-Control": "public, s-maxage=60" } });
}

Proposed fix: the data cache key becomes `dashboard:${userId}` (userId read from the session outside the cached function), /api/dashboard is sent with Cache-Control: private, no-cache, /api/courses keeps public, max-age=0, s-maxage=300, and /api/dashboard is purged at the CDN after the deploy.

Statement: "A test that requests the dashboard as Lan and then as Minh through a simulated CDN, once with the CDN in front and once bypassed, and asserts each learner gets their own data, fails on the release code and passes with this fix."
